[SPOILER="Image transcription"]
[B]Header.[/B] SkinStatues. Any player. Any skin. Any size. 28 poses · up to 128 blocks · by name or by link.

[B]100 blocks tall.[/B] A 100-block statue of Technoblade standing in a generated world.

[B]Any player, any pose.[/B] A row of statues of Vegetta777, Willyrex, elrubius, Mikecrack, Dream and GeorgeNotFound, each in a different pose.

[B]Watch it build.[/B] ElRichMC's statue appearing layer by layer, and a close-up of the second skin layer in relief.

[B]By name or by link.[/B] /statue build DanTDM 40 waving and /statue build https://i.imgur.com/….png 40 pointing_left. Bobicraft built in wool, in concrete and in terracotta.

[B]Features.[/B]
[LIST]
[*]Hollow: only the skin surface is built, so a big statue costs a fraction of the blocks.
[*]Both skin layers: hat, jacket, sleeves and pants in relief, joined to the first layer.
[*]28 poses + your own: poses.yml, extends and mirror.
[*]Undo restores the terrain: every replaced block is saved and put back.
[*]No lag: computed off the main thread, placed in batches per tick.
[*]Anywhere: --at and --facing, from the console, even in far chunks.
[/LIST]

[B]How to start.[/B] 1. Drop the jar in plugins/. 2. /statue build Example 32. 3. network.mojang: true for skins by name, or network.urls: true for links. 4. /statue poses to see every pose.
[/SPOILER]
